\section{Introduction}
Apex-TI is a fully virtualized quantum–topological simulation OS featuring:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
    \item Autonomous solver intelligence (v2.1)
    \item Autonomous cluster intelligence (v3.1)
    \item Virtual Quantum Substrate (v4.0)
    \item ApexIR compiler and optimization suite
\end{itemize}

\section{System Overview}
Apex-TI operates as a distributed, substrate-agnostic physics engine.

\begin{verbatim}
Layer 4: API & Orchestrator Mesh
Layer 3: ApexIR Compiler
Layer 2: Distributed Tensor Fabric
Layer 1: Autonomous Solver Engine
Layer 0: Virtual Quantum Substrate (VQS)
\end{verbatim}

\section{Developer Workflow}
\subsection{Step 1: Define Physics Rules}
Rules are written in high-level ApexIR syntax.

\subsection{Step 2: Compile to ApexIR}
The compiler lowers rules into sparse tensor kernels.

\subsection{Step 3: Execute on Distributed Fabric}
MPI/NCCL partitioning handles large-scale lattice grids.

\subsection{Step 4: Monitor Invariants}
Bott index, Berry curvature, and condition numbers are tracked.

